      "heading": "Distinct real roots",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q": "Solve $y'' - 5y' + 6y = 0$.",
          "answer": "$r^2-5r+6=(r-2)(r-3)=0 \\Rightarrow r = 2, 3$. General solution: $y = C_1e^{2x} + C_2e^{3x}$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Solve $y'' + 2y' - 3y = 0$, $y(0)=1$, $y'(0)=1$.",
          "answer": "$r^2+2r-3=(r+3)(r-1)=0 \\Rightarrow r=-3,1$. So $y=C_1e^{-3x}+C_2e^{x}$. From $y(0)=1$: $C_1+C_2=1$. From $y'(0)=1$: $-3C_1+C_2=1$. Subtracting gives $4C_1=0$, so $C_1=0$, $C_2=1$. Thus $y = e^{x}$."
        }
      ]
